@startuml UC-001-analysis-sequence
!include ../../../diagrams/style.iuml
title UC-001 Configure model connections: analysis sequence diagram

actor Developer
boundary "Configuration Interface" as CI
control "Configure Connection" as Conf
entity "Connection Profile" as CP
boundary "Environment Interface" as EI
control "Call Model" as Call
boundary "Provider Interface" as PI
actor "Model provider" as MP
entity "Model Response" as MR
entity "Connector Error" as CE

note over Developer, CI
  Triggered by a run (UC-006), or by a test
  that builds a connector directly.
end note

Developer -> CI : configure connections(target profile, judge profile)
loop for each profile (target, judge)
  CI -> Conf : settings for "target" (then "judge")
  Conf -> CP : create(name, provider, model, key variable,\nbase URL, timeout, retries, options)
  CP -> CP : validate profile: every setting,\ncollect every problem
  opt 2a: a setting is missing, blank, unknown or out of range
    CP --> Conf : every problem, at once
    Conf --> Developer : profile error "connection 'target': ..." listing every problem
  end
  Conf -> Conf : choose connector(provider), with the profile's options
  opt 3a, 3b: unknown provider, or an option the connector does not accept
    Conf --> Developer : profile error listing the known providers,\nor naming the provider and the unsupported option
  end
  Conf -> EI : resolve credential: read variable(key variable name)
  alt the key is set
    EI --> Conf : key, trimmed
    Conf -> Call : configure(model, key, base URL,\ntimeout, retries, options)
  else 4a: the key variable is missing, empty or only whitespace
    EI --> Conf : nothing
    Conf --> Developer : auth error naming the variable, never its value
  end
end
Conf --> Developer : a connector for the target and one for the judge
note right of Conf
  Every error happens before
  anything is sent.
end note

== later, for each prompt (UC-003, UC-004) ==

[-> Call : call(prompt, instructions)
Call -> PI : one request, instructions\nin the provider's own way
PI -> MP : model request(prompt, instructions, model)
alt the model answers
  MP --> PI : answer, served model, usage, request id
  PI --> Call : answer, served model,\nfinish reason, usage, request id
  Call -> MR : record response(text, requested and served model,\nfinish reason, truncated, token counts, request id)
  [<-- Call : model response
else 6a: the model refuses
  MP --> PI : refusal
  PI --> Call : refusal, served model, finish reason, usage, request id
  Call -> MR : record response(refusal, ...)
  [<-- Call : model response (a refusal is not an error)
else 5a: the provider rejects the request, or cannot be reached
  MP --> PI : HTTP error or timeout
  PI --> Call : failure
  Call -> CE : raise connector error(kind: auth, quota, rate limit,\nunavailable or request; HTTP status, request id)
  [<-- Call : connector error
else 6b: the reply cannot be trusted
  MP --> PI : unusable reply (not a completion, no choices,\nneither an answer nor a refusal)
  PI --> Call : reply
  Call -> CE : raise connector error(kind: response)
  [<-- Call : connector error
end

note right of CE
  Business rule: a failure is always a Connector
  Error of a known kind, with no secret (AC-001-06,
  AC-001-08). A refusal is a Model Response (AC-001-04).
end note
@enduml
